Ono-Sendai — third-party licences
=================================

The `ono` binary links the crates listed below. This file reproduces what each of them
ships about its own licence, because MIT asks that its permission notice travel with the
software, Apache-2.0 §4 that its text travel with a derivative work, and
CDLA-Permissive-2.0 §2.1 that its text travel with the data. Ono-Sendai's own crates are
not here: they are under `LICENSE` beside this file.

It is generated from `Cargo.lock` — `cargo run -p xtask -- licenses --write` — and
`spec-check` regenerates it and compares, so it cannot fall behind a dependency change
(ADR-0608). What it covers is every crate reachable from `ono-cli` as a normal or a
build dependency, over every platform the lockfile resolves: a superset of what any one
build links, which is the safe direction for a notice. Test-only dependencies are absent,
because they are not distributed.

342 crates, carrying 191 distinct licence documents.


